# Each White Ward spares only itself (CR 702.16n: "this Aura") and is white from the start (CR 105.3). One cannot be cast
# onto a creature the other already enchants (protection from white, CR 702.16b), but two Auras entering at once each
# choose a creature that is still unprotected (CR 303.4f), and then each is protected-from by the other's effect: both
# go to the graveyard together (CR 702.16c, 704.5m) with no colour change. Bot1's Devoted Hero and Bot2's Devoted Hero
# each wear a White Ward; Pyroclasm kills both Heroes and so both Wards (Bot2's Yoked Ox survives it), and Second Sunrise
# returns the Heroes and both Wards at once, the Wards onto the Ox, the only creature there to choose. `Attached` and
# `LeftBattlefield` show that both Wards entered attached to the Ox and then left it, rather than staying in the
# graveyard for want of a creature to enchant (CR 303.4g).

